Z||000007||Homicidal||11-08-2001||01:29 AM||||Same problem, took it to a place, they said my shocks + struts are shot.<P>So I'm draggin it in tomorrow to fix it.  I'll keep you updated.||||reg||1
Z||000008||tesmith66||11-08-2001||09:33 AM||||Does it dart from side to side when you get on the brakes? Take a look at the upper control arm bushings. When they deteriorate, the upper arm can move front to rear, causing an abrupt caster change that will make the car want to dart left or right. It will also do this a bit over dips in the pavement. <P>Worn rack bushings can cause a clunking noise when steering or going over irregular pavement and make the car wander at speed.<P>Had the same problem on an '86 SE, fixed it with new bushings. (I actually replaced EVERY bushing on the car with polyurethane)<P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR>Timothy E. Smith<BR>1986 SE V6<BR>1984 Coupe||||reg||4
Z||000009||fastback87||11-08-2001||12:06 PM||||Hey fierochic, you got a bigger pic??  :-)<P>Seriously though, My car did the same thing and it was the rack had a loose bushing on the drivers side (i replaced the hole thing).  It also had a bad upper ball joint on the passenger side.  I replaced that and it is near perfect now, just needs an alignment.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jncomutt||11-08-2001||09:19 PM||||Well my car pulls to the right, BAD.  Had it aligned 3 times (2ce in one day, then next morning)  Had all 4 tires remounted and balanced.  Went through a full suspension check and they still couldn't find anything wrong.  <P>Still pulls, still fustrated, still don't know why....||||reg||1
